---
metadata:
  tags: [archive]
  layout:
    atmosphere: nocturne
---
@view EnemyCard({ enemy }) {
  ::: status {.enemy-card}
  **{{ enemy.name }}**

  HP: {{ enemy.hp }} / {{ enemy.maxHp }}

  @if (enemy.hp <= 0) {
    *It has remembered its name.*
  }
  :::
}

:: Start [start] {"title":"01 / The Nocturne Archive","layout":{"column":"reading","accent":"brass"}}
@action takeKey {
  @do $hasKey = true;
  @do $insight += 1;
  @do $log.push({id: $log.length, text: "You accepted the brass key from the archivist."});
}

# The Nocturne Archive

THE NOCTURNE ARCHIVE / CHAPTER 01

The clock stopped at midnight. **{{ $player.name }}**, this archive keeps not books,
but the things people forgot they once knew.

::: dialogue {speaker="Irene" mood="calm"}
“The name is not important. What matters is whether you will read it again.”
:::

@if (!$hasKey) {
  A [brass key]{.warning} rests on the desk. Its back bears a nearly forgotten word:
  *gneh3-*.

  [[Take the key => takeKey]]
} @else {
  You close your hand around the key. The archive's northern door can now open.
}

[[Enter the reading room - Karlowe -> ReadingRoom]]

[[Enter the vault - Sugarcast -> Vault]]

@region notes {
  *This notes region belongs to one Fragment instance. JavaScript can replace it
  without manipulating the DOM.*
}

@EnemyCard({ enemy: $enemy })

:: FieldNotes {"title":"04 / Traveler's notes"}
# Traveler's notes

@each (event of $log; key event.id) {
  - {{ event.text }}
}

[[Return to the entrance -> Start]]

:: Status {"nav":false}
Known things: **$insight**. Key: {{ $hasKey ? "held" : "not yet found" }}.
